\name{cellucid_view_keep}
\alias{cellucid_view_keep}
\title{Keep the view}
\usage{
cellucid_view_keep(viewer, branch)
}
\arguments{
\item{viewer}{A viewer \code{\link{cellucid_view}()} or \code{\link{cellucid_serve}()} returned.}
\item{branch}{A branch of the tracker in use, by its name: the kept view shows what the selected view shows at its last step (colouring, filters, hidden cells, camera). Text (at least 1 character). Left out unless given (the viewer then chooses as its own control does).}
}
\value{
A \code{cellucid_action_request}, at once and invisibly: the action is sent now, or when the viewer's channel opens.
\code{\link{cellucid_action_result}(request)} returns its outcome (what it did, as names, counts and ids), or \code{NULL} when it had nothing to report; \code{request$step} is the history step it made.
}
\description{
Freeze the selected view as a panel of the multiview, with its colouring, filters and camera, and select it; with a branch, the view as it is at the last step of that branch of the history (to compare branches side by side).
}
\details{
The viewer's action \code{view.keep} (Views). It changes what the viewer shows: one step of the viewer's history, labelled as R's, undone like any other. The state it can change: \code{views}, \code{active-field}, \code{filters}, \code{colors}, \code{visibility}, \code{camera}.
}
\seealso{
\code{\link{cellucid_act}()} sends any action by its type, and \code{\link{cellucid_action_result}()}
collects its answer.
}
\examples{
if (interactive() && requireNamespace("SeuratObject", quietly = TRUE)) {
  data("pbmc_small", package = "SeuratObject")
  viewer <- cellucid_view(SeuratObject::UpdateSeuratObject(pbmc_small))
  request <- cellucid_view_keep(viewer)
  print(request)
  # cellucid_action_result(request) waits for its outcome.
  cellucid_stop(viewer)
}
}
